-- Migration 1919 — withdraw 131 stance chairs from the absence tier-B TAIL BAND (score < 0.50).
--
-- WHAT THIS IS. The last of the three tier-B bands, and the one the ranker could not see. 247 rows,
-- all of them now read by hand: 217 in this pass plus the 30-row measurement sample read earlier
-- under the same standard. Result: **131/247 = 53.0%**.
--
-- 🔴🔴 THE PLAN FOR THIS BAND WAS WRONG AND THE MEASUREMENT OVERTURNED IT. An early 9-row sample
-- came back 0 of 9, and the written advice was to deprioritise the bottom third. A fresh 30-row
-- sample then came back 16 of 30; the full read confirms it at 131 of 247. 0 of 9 has a 95%
-- interval running to 30% — it was never evidence that the tail was clean.
--
--   >= 0.80 → 80.8% (mig 1917) · 0.50-0.80 → 62.1% (mig 1918) · **< 0.50 → 53.0% (here)**
--
-- ⚖⚖ WHY THE RANKER MISSED IT, WHICH IS THE FINDING WORTH KEEPING. The model was fitted on the 307
-- hand-read tier-A rows, where EVERY row lacks evidence, so it learned the shapes of ABSENCE
-- (a non-co-sponsorship, a bare rating, an affiliation). Its KEEP-side features — a named
-- instrument, a date, a questionnaire, a magnitude — are exactly what a RUNG-TEXT row HAS. A row
-- whose evidence is real, dated, the person's own and on-axis, and is mapped to the WRONG RUNG,
-- therefore scores LOW and is still a defect. 🔑 A ranker fitted on one defect class cannot rank a
-- second, and its confidence is ANTI-correlated with it. RUNGTEXT's share of blanks rises as the
-- score falls: 12% in the top band, 24% in the middle, **34% here**, where it is the largest shape.
-- (The 16-row sample had estimated 56% for RUNGTEXT; all 131 blanks put it at 34%. Still first,
-- still rising, and the small sample overstated it.)
--
-- ⚖ ADJUDICATED UNDER `C:/ev-stance-work/absence/STANDARD.md`, the written rule derived from the
-- tier-A ledger's own 101 KEEP rulings and validated at 92% agreement on 24 fresh blind rows.
-- The rows were read in TOPIC order rather than score order, because a topic's rung-mapping errors
-- repeat and the ranker's order carries no information about this defect class.
--
-- ⚖ WHAT A BLANK HERE ASSERTS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT. It asserts that the row's own reasoning does
-- not support the chair it carries. It does NOT assert the person holds no view. Each row records
-- WHICH KIND of nothing it is.
--
-- 🔑 WHY A SEASON 2 BLANK. Season 1 is closed. A Season 2 answer of 0 SUPPRESSES — `NULLIF(pa.value,
-- 0)`, the guard outside the season collapse. Same mechanism as migrations 1914-1918.
--
-- COMPOSITION. 131 rows across 119 people. 119 INSERT, 12 UPDATE.
-- THE SHAPES: RUNGTEXT 44 · AFFIRM 25 · OFFAXIS 24 · ADMITS 15 · NONCOSP 7 · AWAY 6 · AFFIL 6 · SCORE 3 · BODY 1.
--
-- 📐 WHAT THE TOPIC ORDER SHOWED. The defect rate is a property of the LADDER as much as of the
-- row. Where a rung states a broad direction, the evidence usually describes it and the row keeps:
-- abortion 27% blanked, climate 20%, healthcare 20%, residential-zoning 0 of 5. Where a rung states
-- a specific MECHANISM or exception framework that a general record cannot reach, the rows fail:
-- deportation 9 of 9, ai-regulation 3 of 3, public-safety-approach 6 of 7, same-sex-marriage 7 of 9,
-- trans-athletes 9 of 12, fossil-fuels 15 of 21. Two ladders are worth a Season 3 look on this
-- evidence: social-security rung 3 reads "make small adjustments to both benefits and taxes", so it
-- has NO rung for the common position of defending the programme as it stands (8 of 12 blanked);
-- and the trans-athletes ladder lands every pro-inclusion record on rung 2's "after completing basic
-- documentation of their transition", a clause almost nobody has ever stated.
-- ⚖ The same sentence can keep on one ladder and blank on another, correctly: Coester's "Medicaid
-- and Social Security will be protected" KEEPS at medicare/aid rung 3 ("improve current programs")
-- and BLANKS at social-security rung 3, which asks for adjustments he never proposed.
--
-- ⚠ NOT BLANKED — 116 of the 247. The clearest keeps name an instrument whose CONTENT is the rung's
-- own distinguishing clause: Roys's bill repealing Wisconsin's public-plan abortion coverage ban
-- (chair 1's "publicly funded"), Barragán's quoted "the state must stop issuing new drilling
-- permits", Piedmont-Smith's co-authorship of the UDO's 15% inclusionary requirement, Bonta's AB 32
-- and bail reform, Nikema Williams's roll call with the childcare provisions itemised.
-- ⚠ Two KEEPs are explicitly PROVISIONAL and routed, not cleared: Scott Brown's healthcare row
-- rests on 2006-2012 evidence (migration 1916 already overturned another of his rows), and Eric
-- Schmitt's tariffs row cites S.J.Res. 77 with a date that looks wrong. Vintage and a bad date are
-- repair work, not an absence, and this migration does not touch them.
--
-- Applied by hand via psql; no migration runner exists in this repo, so "applied" means its data
-- effects are live. Guards below fail the whole transaction rather than write a partial result.

